From: minisandbox <minisandbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/pvm: register late E820 resources without PCI

x86 leaves non-busy E820 resources, including legacy persistent memory,
for e820__reserve_resources_late() after PCI resource survey.  A minimal PVM
guest intentionally builds without PCI, so the survey and late registration
never occur and e820_pmem cannot discover a memmap=nn!ss range.

There is no PCI address space to survey in this configuration.  Register the
remaining resources immediately after the initial E820 pass so the native
e820_pmem and pmem drivers can expose the host-enforced read-only range.

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c b/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
@@ -1163,6 +1163,14 @@ void __init setup_arch(char **cmdline_p)
 	x86_init.hyper.guest_late_init();
 
 	e820__reserve_resources();
+	/*
+	 * minisandbox: PVM guests deliberately omit PCI, whose resource
+	 * survey normally performs the late registration needed for E820
+	 * type-12 persistent memory.  No PCI resources can conflict here.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PVM_GUEST) && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI))
+		e820__reserve_resources_late();
+
 	e820__register_nosave_regions(max_pfn);
 
 	x86_init.resources.reserve_resources();
-- 
